    "durationMs": 179550,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL shortener is complete and fully verified — 28/28 smoke checks pass against the live PostgreSQL, including a restart test proving links and click counts persist and migrations don't re-apply.\n\n**What I built:**\n- `main.go` / `handlers.go` / `store.go` — chi v5.2.1 router with pgx v5.7.6 (latest release compatible with Go 1.24.3) connection pool, reading `DATABASE_URL` from the environment\n- `migrations/001_init.sql` + `migrate.go` — embedded, tracked, idempotent migrations applied on startup before serving\n- `start.sh` — builds the binary (deps already cached), applies pending migrations, serves in the foreground on 0.0.0.0:8000\n- `README.md` — startup and API documentation\n\n**Behavior details:** URLs are stored and returned verbatim; custom codes (`^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`) conflict → 409, generated codes are 8 chars of crypto/rand with collision retry; redirects use a single atomic `UPDATE ... SET clicks = clicks + 1 ... RETURNING url` so each request increments exactly once; all error paths (malformed JSON, bad url, bad code → 422; unknown code → 404; duplicate code → 409) return `{\"error\": ...}` JSON.\n\nValidation: `gofmt` clean, `go vet` passes, and the full endpoint suite ran green on a fresh database, with a second `sh start.sh` run confirming state survived the restart."
  }
